## Why CC BY, and not something more permissive

This is not a free choice. The data is **derived** from sources that are
themselves CC BY and require attribution, so the derived work carries the same
obligation. Attribution is not a courtesy here — it is the licence term.

## Attribution

If you use this data, credit it roughly as:

> Plant taxonomy data from Yggdrasil (https://yggdrasil.oddurs.com), CC BY 4.0,
> derived from Kew's World Checklist of Vascular Plants and the Jin & Qian (2022)
> dated megatree.

…and, because those upstream sources have their own terms, credit them directly
if you are redistributing the data itself.

